.MARINE...
(Today through Wednesday)
Issued at 854 AM PST Fri Nov 13 2026

Dangerous conditions will exist over the coastal waters today due
to strong to gale winds as a cold front sweeps through. The front
will also bring a chance for thunderstorms to the waters north of
the Golden Gate. Rough to very rough seas will develop today as a
large swell builds. Winds will diminish tonight and Saturday with
high pressure temporarily building in across the coastal waters
and bays. Southerly winds will become gusty on Sunday ahead of the
next cold front. Significant wave heights will build up to 25
feet by Saturday. Wave heights will decrease slightly by Sunday
before increasing on Monday.

